A “descendant” of node p means every node strictly below it (children, grandchildren, etc.), not including p.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------

function countDescendants(T, p):

    // Base case: no node means no descendants
    if p is null:
        return 0

    total = 0     // Stores the total number of descendants of p

    // If a left child exists, it is a descendant
    // Add 1 for the child, plus all of its descendants
    if T.left(p) is not null:
        total = total + 1 + countDescendants(T, T.left(p))

    // If a right child exists, it is also a descendant
    // Add 1 for the child, plus all of its descendants
    if T.right(p) is not null:
        total = total + 1 + countDescendants(T, T.right(p))

    // Return the total number of descendants of p
    return total

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This uses only:

- Left(p)
- Right(p)
- and counts each child as a descendant (+1) plus all descendants of that child (recursive call).